# s2-assets database migration one-shot job container (Feature 001, T037).
#
# Authority:
# - specs/001-application-foundation/tasks.md T037
# - Product Owner Stage B authorization & Stage A feasibility report
# - TECHNOLOGY.md §6 & §9 (explicit reviewable migrations before API startup)
#
# Scoped Resource Ownership (R3):
# - ContainerName=s2-assets-api-migration scopes container execution to this project.
# - Secret=s2-assets-database-url scopes the database connection secret.
# - Unit Exclusivity: Governed by api-migration.service within this user's systemd session.
#
# Lifecycle Contract & Fail-Closed PostgreSQL Prerequisite (B2):
# - Dependencies: Wants=postgres.service and After=postgres.service.
#   Wants= orders startup after postgres.service without coupling the retained gate state:
#   if postgres.service is subsequently restarted or stopped for maintenance, systemd does NOT
#   stop api-migration.service or clear its retained 'active (exited)' state.
# - Start-Time Fail-Closed Prerequisite:
#   ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/systemctl --user is-active --quiet postgres.service
#   Because systemd Wants=/After= permits startup even if the wanted service fails or times out,
#   ExecStartPre asserts that postgres.service has reached 'active' state (driven by Notify=healthy).
#   - If postgres.service failed or timed out: ExecStartPre exits non-zero (code 3), failing
#     the start job immediately, marking api-migration.service as 'failed', and suppressing
#     ExecStart=. The migration CLI is NEVER executed against an unhealthy/unready database.
#   - Because api-migration.service is in 'failed' state, api.service's Requisite= check fails closed,
#     blocking API startup.
#   - If postgres.service is active: ExecStartPre exits 0 and ExecStart= executes the migration CLI.
# - Execution: Type=oneshot, RemainAfterExit=yes, Restart=no.
#   Foreground execution captures CLI exit status directly:
#   - Exit 0: transitions to 'active (exited)', satisfying Requisite= for api.service.
#   - Non-zero exit: transitions to 'failed', blocking api.service.
#
# Controlled Release Rollout Protocol (B2):
# - Paired Artifact Discipline: Every production release pairs an immutable API image
#   (e.g., localhost/s2-assets-api:<tag/digest>) with its matching migration image
#   (e.g., localhost/s2-assets-migration:<tag/digest>) built from the exact same commit.
# - Prohibited: Changing artifact selection (updating Image=) under a retained successful gate.
#   In systemd, updating Quadlet files and reloading daemons does NOT invalidate an existing
#   'active (exited)' state; an outdated gate must never permit a new API version to launch.
# - Rollout Sequence:
#   1. Invalidate Old Gate: 'systemctl --user stop api-migration.service'
#      Transitions gate to 'inactive', ensuring api.service cannot start prematurely.
#   2. Update Image References: Update Image= in api-migration.container and api.container.
#   3. Reload Daemon: 'systemctl --user daemon-reload'
#   4. Execute Matching Migration: 'systemctl --user start api-migration.service'
#      ExecStartPre validates postgres.service active; new migration runs to completion.
#      Failure / Retry: If migration fails, investigate logs (journalctl --user -u api-migration.service),
#      resolve the underlying issue, and retry 'systemctl --user start api-migration.service'.
#   5. Roll Out API: Once migration reaches 'active (exited)', run 'systemctl --user restart api.service'.
[Unit]
Description=s2-assets database migration one-shot job
Wants=postgres.service
After=postgres.service

[Container]
ContainerName=s2-assets-api-migration
Image=localhost/s2-assets-migration:t037
Network=s2-assets.network
Exec=node src/migrator.ts latest
EnvironmentFile=./api-migration.env
Secret=s2-assets-database-url,type=env,target=DATABASE_URL

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=yes
Restart=no
ExecStartPre=/usr/bin/systemctl --user is-active --quiet postgres.service
